  "relevance_note": "An exploratory CVID DNA-methylation study whose CD14+ monocyte discovery cohort includes one identifiable TNFAIP3 carrier analysed individually (\"one CVID patient was later found to carry a monogenic TNFAIP3 variant\"; \"we performed a separate pathway analysis of this individual’s monocytes\").",
  "method_note": "Read the whole paper by hand; no script transcribed any table (the script only assembled the JSON). Scope: the only in-scope person is the single TNFAIP3 carrier among the three CD14+ CVID patients of the WGBS discovery cohort. The other five discovery-cohort patients (no monogenic variant found) and the 60-patient plasma cohort (no genetic results reported) are out of scope. No relatives are described. Label: the paper uses descriptions ('the TNFAIP3 carrier', 'this individual', 'this patient') rather than an identifier, so rule 6 ('unnamed person 1') was applied. No variant description is printed: the paper says only that 'This TNFAIP3 variant was first described in a CVID patient in 2020 (34)', so variant_original_string is 'not reported'. The paper never uses the terms HA20 or haploinsufficiency. Pathogenicity: authors call it a 'monogenic TNFAIP3 variant'; 'No other CVID patients in this cohort had pathogenic variants' implies, without stating it, that they regard it as pathogenic. Ref (34) is cited for an earlier description of the variant in a CVID patient. The paper does not say it is the same patient, so cites_prior_report_of_same_patients is null. cohort_size_as_stated = 6, the stated total for the epigenetic analyses, where the carrier was found and the gene panel applied. The separate plasma cohort of 60 CVID patients (no overlap) is not counted, and the authors never state a combined total. Individual sex and age are not reported: Table 1 gives only group values (CD14 CVID: 1 female of 3; mean age 35, range 22-46). 'Autoimmune/inflammatory complications' is recorded as observed from explicit statements about all six discovery-cohort patients (inferred from group statement). Which specific complication this person had is not stated, so every checklist item is 'not reported'. Statements that at inclusion 'none had acute infection or exacerbation of a chronic infection, and none received prophylactic antibiotics or immunosuppressive therapy, apart from Ig replacement' mirror the study's enrolment criteria, so they were not used as feature or treatment evidence (v3 study-criteria rule). treatment_summary is 'not reported'. The functional_evidence_statement records the individual methylation pathway analysis of the carrier's monocytes; this is not a direct functional assay of the variant. study_type set to 'other' (exploratory case-control methylation/plasma study); 'case series/cohort' is arguable. No internal contradictions about this person found.",
